Z||000000||fix||08-10-2001||09:13 PM||||I'm looking to replace my gauges with digital ones from cyberdyne or intellitronix.  I question, however, if the stock fiero speedometer sender will work with these gauges.  Does anyone know if it will?  I think the sender that you can buy with the digital gauges won't work on a fiero tranny so that's why I ask.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||08-10-2001||10:02 PM||||I don't know if the Fiero VSS will work, but if not, you can get a cable drive from a Cavalier trans. The Cyberdyne VSS will screw onto it. Cyberdyne uses a Ford type VSS, and I'd imagine that Intellitronix does too because they were once the same company.<P>I almost forgot, If you find a Cavalier with factory cruise control, it will have the cable drive for the speedometer, <B>AND</B> the electric VSS output to feed the ECM. Not sure of the pulses/mile of the Cavalier VSS, but judging by the connector it is an optical sensor.<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Jay||08-10-2001||10:47 PM||||I'm not sure about on a stock fiero but I've got Cyberdyne speedo on my Northstar Fiero and it didn't need any special sender.  I used the stock one from the caddy.  Give them a call, they know their stuff.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
